==============================================================================
S701: Is the self-conjugate runner n/2 load-bearing in AP_n? (even n)
==============================================================================
Convention: AP_n = {1,...,n-1}, n-1 runners, conjectured floor M=1/n.
R_n = AP_n \ {n/2} = negation-symmetric, n-2 runners, floor >= 1/(n-1).

--- n = 4  (n/2 = 2) ---
  M(AP_n)            = 1/4   (1/n = 1/4)  argmax t = {1/4, 3/4}
      t=1/4: binders=[1, 3]
      t=3/4: binders=[1, 3]
  n/2 ever a binder of AP_n? False    unique binder? False
  M(R_n)=M(AP_n\{2}) = 1/2 = 0.500000   (1/(n-1)=1/3=0.333333)
      argmax t = {1/2}
        t=1/2: binders=[1, 3]   ||(n/2)t||=0
  n/2 LOAD-BEARING (M(AP)<M(R))? True    dist of n/2 at R-optima: [Fraction(0, 1)]

--- n = 6  (n/2 = 3) ---
  M(AP_n)            = 1/6   (1/n = 1/6)  argmax t = {1/6, 5/6}
      t=1/6: binders=[1, 5]
      t=5/6: binders=[1, 5]
  n/2 ever a binder of AP_n? False    unique binder? False
  M(R_n)=M(AP_n\{3}) = 1/3 = 0.333333   (1/(n-1)=1/5=0.200000)
      argmax t = {1/3, 2/3}
        t=1/3: binders=[1, 2, 4, 5]   ||(n/2)t||=0
        t=2/3: binders=[1, 2, 4, 5]   ||(n/2)t||=0
  n/2 LOAD-BEARING (M(AP)<M(R))? True    dist of n/2 at R-optima: [Fraction(0, 1)]

